    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">Four Alberta Securities Commission leaders on how regulation is adapting to a changing capital market.

On October 27, <a class="link" href="https://ca.linkedin.com/in/katrina-prokopy-15a13032?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Katrina Prokopy</a>, <a class="link" href="https://ca.linkedin.com/in/lynn-tsutsumi-0a048530?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Lynn Tsutsumi</a>, and Denise Weeres joins <a class="link" href="https://ca.linkedin.com/in/samir-sabharwal-87531ba?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Samir Sabharwal</a> on the ASC Connect stage to discuss "Evolution in our capital market: The ASC’s perspective"

Register now and secure your seat at ASC Connect: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/e-fiCVhA?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/e-fiCVhA</a>

Your registration includes a breakfast buffet, a catered networking lunch, a cocktail reception, and a full day of discussion with the people shaping what comes next.</p>
